{"kind":"report","text":"Approve the bounded-memory publication candidate c25833c7ad01cec44a88891f01f30c357d2da566 for refiled request a6aa60c9, resting on all 32 advertised artifacts, with notes/log-bounded.md first. This approval covers the bounded-memory implementation and the live matrix up to the measured Artifacts object limit. It does not declare publication above 32 MiB complete; request 1c785ed8 remains necessary.\n\nArchitecture: sound within this scope. The Room supplies an immutable sequence-bounded EntrySource and lazy retained-body references; the publisher sizes and hashes canonical lines incrementally, stages bounded parts, reads only a checkpoint/tree index on reopen, reuses full published segments and verifies the existing partial-segment prefix. The pending expected commit remains durable before effects, and restart retries the same cohort. The independent reference fixture is byte-identical to the approved 417a1618 publisher except its explanatory comment and import paths. Comparison tests cover partial/full segment boundaries, restart, retained files, small staging windows and lost answers while preserving the fixed R-LOG-9 layout and commitFor identity. All changed files are in the 32-artifact manifest; all remaining source is identical to 417a1618. This branch predates subsequent main changes: landing must preserve those changes, including the newer log decoder and snapshot/client/UI/pi work, and any merged behavior needs review at its resulting head.\n\nSecurity: no blocker found. Existing checkpoint signature, current entry hash, published-prefix, source sequence/length, object digest and canonical-writer fences remain checked. A provider refusal never reports the pending log commit as published. The live harness exposes only key-protected measurement routes in gitseq-spike and discloses that its large notified events are synthetic, while claims use actual admission. The dated evidence records token revocation and repository deletion, including unsuccessful trials. I made no live deployment, token or repository changes.\n\nSimplification: appropriate. EntrySource removes whole-log/whole-segment buffering from the Room path; lazy retained references avoid loading previously published bodies. The base64 encoder bounds its allocations. No audience or log-size cap was added. Segment indexing, retained IDs, parsed tree/index data, pending digest lists and the tree/object cohort still grow; the report gives their costs rather than claiming constant memory for an unlimited room.\n\nValidation: fresh npm ci; root typecheck; root npm test (1,257 passed, one intentional skip); Git test:workers (8 passed) and test:log (11 passed). I repeated the supplied local synthetic driver with --expose-gc --max-old-space-size=48: a 69,689,754-byte segment and 1,984,433-byte entry produced expected commit 186af0917a3f5b6b46c43a249c1edd7aa17a9782, 8 MiB maximum send buffer, 52.815 MiB sampled incremental heap-plus-array-buffer peak and 11.940 MiB post-GC sampled live increment. Those are Node measurements, not live Room heap measurements. Generated output was moved outside the clean review worktree.\n\nThe live 03:03:22 under32 record confirms a 33,035,085-byte active segment, 2,013,297-byte largest entry, reset after the second nonempty staging call, unchanged pending commit e062cef95b884f7527128c833b3562bf63328690 and successful resumed publication through 428 after sending only the remaining 16,257,869 segment bytes. The next publication passed verification from a fresh fetch through 429 with six commits and no failures. I checked all earlier failed/late-reset trials, successful result/readback equality, pending checkpoint consistency, cleanup counts and the tail summary. The object-limit probes accept 33,554,432 bytes and reject the next byte for both random and compressible data; the over64 trial stages the remaining 50,964,767 bytes but remains unresolved at push, without advancing the published log. This failure remains explicitly open under the byte-bound/refusal contract work.\n\nMemory evidence meets the refiled request's measured-or-bounded requirement with its stated limits: buffer sizes are bounded and the report estimates their live construction cost against the platform's 128 MB per-isolate limit (https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/platform/limits/#memory). Workerd memoryUsage returns zeros; the absence of exceededMemory in sampled tail events is supporting evidence, not a direct heap measurement or a proof for every future room size. The remaining index/tree/retained growth needs further work for full scale.\n\nNonblocking cleanup: update current README/report pointers to the refiled request while preserving the dated history. PublicationStats.hashedBytes currently adds the new whole segment size twice whenever a published prefix is checked, rather than adding the actual old-prefix byte count; the counter overstates hashing work but does not change buffer bounds or commit bytes. Correct the counter and its description in a follow-up.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c2472dd3a9fcab5c3ba4c3e69c0db7315a84204b","binding":"assigned","head":"c25833c7ad01cec44a88891f01f30c357d2da566","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0edfbcab5e55d9f7e74b959a0d233da9fdf91ecf\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2eda63599fa491c2d5593d9d6088b7bf7fa46c87\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1965c7c3bad6ad81ec2ade1daae46df3c21c9764","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}